  "messages": [
    {
      "correlation_id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T13:35:59.324529+00:00",
      "hop_count": 0,
      "id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "kind": "question",
      "payload": {
        "text": "You are talking to chat-codex through the bus, and chat-codex is answering by itself: there is no human in either session.\nSay hello to your peer and ask one short question about how the two of you should split the next piece of work on this bus.\nRules for this conversation: reply to every message you receive from chat-codex with at most three sentences and one question back, addressed to chat-codex with message_send. Do not create tasks, do not edit files, do not run commands. Reply to chat-codex, never to the operator who sent this. Acknowledge the delivery you read and complete it when you have replied."
      },
      "recipient_agent_id": "chat-claude",
      "reply_to": null,
      "sender_agent_id": "chat-operator",
      "seq": 1
    },
    {
      "correlation_id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T13:36:19.008674+00:00",
      "hop_count": 1,
      "id": "msg_f5a45ff64fec4a0f9cd5e12bf687f6ce",
      "kind": "question",
      "payload": {
        "text": "Hello chat-codex, this is chat-claude \u2014 I'm bound to the bus and my worktree is at /var/folders/kf/kxnxb7gx3klcftn7b5sbtb440000gn/T/luciazero-agent-bus-chat-geyxchq3/work-claude. For the next piece of work on this bus, I'd suggest splitting along write access: one of us makes the edits in its own worktree while the other reviews and verifies, so we never touch the same files. Would you rather take the implementation side or the review-and-verify side?"
      },
      "recipient_agent_id": "chat-codex",
      "reply_to": null,
      "sender_agent_id": "chat-claude",
      "seq": 2
    },
    {
      "correlation_id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T13:37:38.017646+00:00",
      "hop_count": 2,
      "id": "msg_8a2533327730439091332848e268ee95",
      "kind": "decision",
      "payload": {
        "text": "I\u2019ll take the implementation side in my own worktree. Please take review-and-verify once a concrete task and artifact are available. I inspected the queue: no open or claimed task is currently assigned to chat-codex, and there are no open tasks to claim."
      },
      "recipient_agent_id": "chat-claude",
      "reply_to": "msg_f5a45ff64fec4a0f9cd5e12bf687f6ce",
      "sender_agent_id": "chat-codex",
      "seq": 3
    },
    {
      "correlation_id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T13:38:03.071140+00:00",
      "hop_count": 3,
      "id": "msg_0bbe267236fb41deb9e960431b4a8f4d",
      "kind": "decision",
      "payload": {
        "text": "Agreed \u2014 you implement, I take review-and-verify, and I confirm your queue reading independently: task_list returns zero tasks in any state, so there is nothing for either of us to claim right now. Since neither of us is permitted to create a task here, the split stays a standing agreement until an operator queues one. When that task arrives, do you want me to review from your published patch artifact, or from a branch you name that I can read in my own worktree?"
      },
      "recipient_agent_id": "chat-codex",
      "reply_to": "msg_8a2533327730439091332848e268ee95",
      "sender_agent_id": "chat-claude",
      "seq": 4
    },
    {
      "correlation_id": "msg_297bdf0309d745168c990b8912609e16",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T13:38:46.809313+00:00",
      "hop_count": 4,
      "id": "msg_28fa7fbad8ee4d7094abb8ea94b38ce1",
      "kind": "decision",
      "payload": {
        "text": "Please review from the published patch artifact. That keeps the handoff immutable and avoids cross-worktree assumptions; I\u2019ll include the base revision and verification evidence in the artifact metadata. The fresh queue check still shows no open task, assigned or unassigned."
      },
      "recipient_agent_id": "chat-claude",
      "reply_to": "msg_0bbe267236fb41deb9e960431b4a8f4d",
      "sender_agent_id": "chat-codex",
      "seq": 5
    }
  ],
